messages:
alex_cs: Heads-up, customer 'Clearline' is seeing large numbers of 429s during onboarding preflight from browsers. Spike started ~09:14 UTC and concentrated in eu-central.
alex_cs: They say user flows open multiple tabs during setup which triggers a lot of simultaneous preflight calls. Example error: `429 Too Many Requests` with headers `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`, `Retry-After: 45`.
cleo_sdk: Can you share the init they shipped? Browser SDK default preflight + no client-side jitter is a classic stampede.
alex_cs: Sanitized snippet they used: ```js
// shipped by Clearline onboarding flow
window.addEventListener('load', async () => {
  const token = await fetch('/api/ephemeral').then(r=>r.json()).then(j=>j.token);
  for (const wf of document.querySelectorAll('.widget')) {
    Redwood.init({ key: token, preflight: true });
  }
});
```
ben_infra: Observed at edge: many ephemeral mint calls clustered in sub-10s windows. Our per-tenant sliding limiter sees bursts and returns 429. No upstream 5xx, purely rate enforcement.
cleo_sdk: Immediate guidance to customer: 1) avoid mint-per-widget; fetch once and reuse for N seconds (eg 30s). 2) cap concurrent preflights (<=3). 3) add randomized stagger (200-800ms). Provide them an example patch.
cleo_sdk: Example client change to send: ```js
const token = await fetch('/api/ephemeral').then(r=>r.json()).then(j=>j.token);
const widgets = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.widget')).slice(0,5);
await Promise.all(widgets.map((w,i) => (async () => {
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200 + Math.random()*600));
  return Redwood.init({ key: token, preflight: true });
})()));
```
tyler_sre: Short-term on our side: I added a tenant-specific soft-splay for Clearline to smooth the incoming mint burst (rule id r-9921). ops-bot, apply config?
ops-bot: applying edge config r-9921 for tenant=clearline -> SUCCESS (eu-central propagation ~18s).
ben_infra: We can also temporarily raise the per-tenant burst allowance for onboarding; will need an ops change and product approval.
cleo_sdk: Also recommended for them: switch to a server-side provisioning pattern for quick onboarding (mint server-side once per user session), and fallback to cached token in case of Retry-After.
alex_cs: I'll send the client patch + mitigation note and request they deploy a canary. If they still see >1% 429 after client changes and splay, we'll proceed with quota bump and runtime prefix-cache fallback.
tyler_sre: Agreed. I'll monitor eu-central token mint logs and set an alert for RejectedMintRate > 0.5% for next 6 hours.
ale x_cs: Thanks team — pinging Clearline now and will update when they confirm. :thumbsup:
